Late Edit
: Good catch by Solar_Flare, see answers below.
Depending on how complex your text is, one work around could be to put the text difference in one or multiple variables/unused actor names, and reference that in your "Message Text" command (you cannot put special text commands in variables, so you would have to splice around those if your text contains some).
You could also replace the "Message Text" and "Show Choices" with script commands (see
MV/MZ script call list
).
You can prevent the interpreter from stopping after the first Message Text by only putting the
this.setWaitMode('message')
line in the last command:
